aplasia cell"], "both are MUC6+ PGC+ TFF2+ mucous gland cells; Oliver 2024 explicitly says the metaplastic MGN-like cells 'phenotypically resemble cells of the Brunner's glands'. Brunner's glands are a NORMAL duodenal submucosal structure; the metaplastic population appears in INFLAMED ileum/colon and adds AQP5, BPIFB1 and the inflammatory genes DUOX2/LCN2/CEACAM7."], ["enteric inhibitory motor neuron vs enteric secretomotor neuron", ["enteric inhibitory motor neuron", "enteric secretomotor neuron"], "VIP and GAL are shared: Drokhlyansky 2020 annotates PIMN subsets 'based on co-expression of Nos1 and Vip' but also lists 'PSVNs (n = 48 genes; e.g. Vip, Gal, Scgn, Calb2)'. NOS1 is the inhibitory-motor discriminator; SCGN/CALB2 the secretomotor one."], ["enteric inhibitory motor neuron vs interstitial cell of Cajal (ETV1)", ["enteric inhibitory motor neuron"], "ETV1 is in the PIMN shared program (Drokhlyansky 2020) AND is a required marker of interstitial cells of Cajal in this wing. KIT/ANO1 are ICC-exclusive; NOS1/GFRA1 + the pan-neuronal PHOX2B/ELAVL4 are neuron-exclusive."], ["enteric sensory neuron vs type D enteroendocrine cell (SST)", ["enteric sensory neuron"], "SST is in the PSN shared program and is the D-cell defining hormone. CALCB/NMU/NOG + PHOX2B/ELAVL4 -> neuron; CHGA/CHGB/NEUROD1 + EPCAM -> EEC."], ["Paneth cell vs BEST4+ cell / follicle-associated epithelium (LYZ)", ["Paneth cell"], "Burclaff 2022 shows LYZ is expressed by BEST4+ cells and highly by FAE, and reports that cells called Paneth cells in an earlier scRNA-seq study 'are actually BEST4+ cells'. DEFA5/DEFA6/ITLN2/PLA2G2A are the human PC markers."], ["activated CD8-positive alpha-beta T cell vs CD8 intraepithelial lymphocyte / tissue-resident memory CD8 T cell", ["CD8 intra-epithelial lymphocyte"], "There is no clean one. CD69/GZMA/GZMB/NKG7 are ALREADY the supporting set of the wing's CD8 intraepithelial lymphocyte Term (residency / constitutive cytotoxic programme), and CD69+CD103+ is the adult human intestinal Trm phenotype (PMID 33772147, human fetal/infant/adult gut: 'tissue-resident memory CD69+CD103+ CD8 T cells detected in adults'). CD103/CD69 are themselves inflammation-induced Trm differentiation markers (PMID 28380351, mouse). IL2RA/TNFRSF9 are constitutive on other populations and had no human small-intestinal discriminative sentence."]], "oq": ["HUMAN_SMALL_INTESTINE:0000007", "HUMAN_SMALL_INTESTINE:0000031", "HUMAN_SMALL_INTESTINE:0000004", "HUMAN_SMALL_INTESTINE:0000037", "HUMAN_SMALL_INTESTINE:0000038", "HUMAN_SMALL_INTESTINE:0000039", "HUMAN_SMALL_INTESTINE:0000040", "HUMAN_SMALL_INTESTINE:0000041", "HUMAN_SMALL_INTESTINE:0000023", "HUMAN_SMALL_INTESTINE:0000043", "HUMAN_SMALL_INTESTINE:0000010", "HUMAN_SMALL_INTESTINE:0000001"], "ca": [{"name": "small intestinal proximal-distal axis", "applies_to": ["absorptive enterocyte", "enteroendocrine cell", "intestinal epithelial cell"], "poles": [{"pole": "proximal (duodenum/jejunum)", "context_markers": ["TMPRSS15", "MUC6", "PGC", "TFF2", "GIP", "CCK", "SCT", "MLN", "Tmprss15", "Muc6", "Pgc", "Tff2", "Gip", "Cck", "Sct"], "subtypes": {}}, {"pole": "distal (ileum)", "context_markers": ["FABP6", "SLC10A2", "SLC51B", "APOB", "Fabp6", "Slc10a2", "Slc51b", "Apob"], "subtypes": {"absorptive enterocyte": "ileal enterocyte"}}], "pmids": ["35176508", "31753849", "37468586", "37790430", "28462382"]}], "sa": [{"name": "osteoclastogenic RANKL program", "markers": ["TNFSF11", "ETS1"], "pmids": ["40136507", "38554844"], "applies_to": ["mesenchymal cell"], "mimics": [], "anchor_markers": [], "of": []}, {"name": "type 2/22 cytokine program", "markers": ["IL13", "IL22", "IL4", "IL5", "GATA3"], "pmids": ["26242300"], "applies_to": ["T cell"], "mimics": [], "anchor_markers": [], "of": []}, {"name": "proliferating", "markers": ["MKI67", "TOP2A", "CCNB1", "CENPF"], "pmids": ["12058064"], "applies_to": [], "mimics": [], "anchor_markers": [], "of": ["tissue-resident macrophage", "basal keratinocyte", "fibroblast", "c